/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-041/oryon_repo/docs/docs/philosophy.md:18: There is no "research version" and "production version" of a feature. There is one feature, two interfaces. This eliminates research-to-production drift by construction, not by discipline. You don't need code reviews to catch divergence. You don't need integration tests comparing two implementations. The divergence cannot exist because the second implementation does not exist.
